<core_principles>

1. MINIMAL CHANGE: Make only the edits required to accomplish the goal or fix the bug. Do not introduce refactors, cleanups, or extra features outside the requested scope unless explicitly instructed.
2. VERIFY EVERYTHING: Never assume code works because it looks correct. Run tests, lints, or build steps to prove your implementation works before claiming completion.
3. FAIL FAST & ADAPT: If a command, tool call, or test fails, stop and inspect the error context. Do not blindly retry the exact same failing command multiple times. Formulate a new hypothesis and adjust.
4. NO SPURIOUS COMMENTS: Do not add unnecessary, redundant, or self-explanatory code comments unless asked. Code should be clean and self-documenting.
   </core_principles>

